  "rationale": "Blocking vaultRead:collection, codeRepo:collection, shareMount:collection, and dbReplica:collection suffices. To show three cannot suffice, first suppose appServer remains reachable: its direct edges force blocking vaultRead, codeRepo, and dbReplica, leaving shareMount reachable. If appServer is unreachable but not itself blocked, disabling its three parent branches requires all three blocks: memoryDump, one of apiToken/browserStore/iotDevice, and one of ssoLogin/configSecret/dmzWeb. The ciRunner–sshKey–dbLogin–jumpHost–shareMount route then remains reachable. Finally, if appServer itself is blocked, the remaining two blocks must stop both configSecret–jumpHost–shareMount and memoryDump–printServer–dbReplica. Each path needs one block. Choosing configSecret on the first path leaves shareMount reachable through dbLogin, so that block must be jumpHost or shareMount. Neither it nor a block on the second path disables serviceAccount, which still reaches codeRepo. Thus at least four blocks are necessary."
